      "Chunk text:  In total, at least 220 casualties have been reported, with insured loss estimates of approximately EUR150 million-EUR250 million in the Netherlands (Verbond voor Verzekeraars, 2022), GLYPH&lt;24&gt; EUR2.2 billion in Belgium (Assuralia, 2022) and GLYPH&lt;24&gt; EUR8.2 billion (GDV, 2022) in Germany. The event caused major damages to residential and commercial structures and to many critical infrastructure (CI) assets. Not only vital functions for first responders were affected (eg hospitals, fire departments), but also railways, bridges and utility networks (eg water and electricity supply) were severely damaged, expecting to take months to years to fully rebuild.\n",
