      "Processing chunk no. 2 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  Among all the days of the period covered by this study, he highlighted the 29th of October, when very serious impacts occurred, especially in the province of Valencia. That day, the weather factor, extraordinarily extreme, was combined with the hydrological factor and triggered the most tragic natural event in the recent history of our country. 223 people lost their lives (3 still missing at the time of this study) and the economic impact on the main economic sectors would exceed 13 billion euros, according to the Chamber of Valencia (Camera V. 2024).To this figure, the extraordinary losses and deterioration of the infrastructure, as well as the material damage suffered by thousands of families of the populations affected by the floods, the latter translated in 3.5 billion euros, according to estimates of the Consortium of Insurance Compensation (Consorcio CS. 2024). Also this day there were areas of the provinces of Albacete, Cuenca and Malaga where the loss of human life occurred due to the sudden increase of channels, as well as numerous material and infrastructure damages.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
