      "Processing chunk no. 3 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  The presence of a dana towards the Strait area and the transport of moisture from a very warm Mediterranean to the Peninsula caused a great atmospheric instability that led to the development of powerful stormy systems that in the area of Turís (Valencia) left records in our country of precipitation accumulated in one, six and twelve hours. The development of the weather situation and its subsequent evolution are explained in chapter 2 of this report, while in chapter 3 we show a description of the main stormy systems that were generated throughout the days during which the situation of strong instability was maintained.Chapter 4 shows a daily chronology of how rainfall was occurring, highlighting those autonomous communities where rainfall caused the most impact. This chapter also describes the weather warnings that were issued throughout these days for the most affected areas. Finally, chapter 5 shows a short comparative study of rainfall on the 29th day focused on the province of Valencia with respect to three other historical situations of strong socioeconomic impact in this province since 1950.\n",
