      "Chunk text:  In the region of Rhineland-Palatinate (Germany), most drinking water supply was restored within 2 months (Hochwasser Ahr, 2021a). However, sewage treatment plants in Altenahr, Mayschoss and Sinzig had been largely destroyed (Hochwasser Ahr, 2021b), and it is expected to take at least 1.5 years to fully repair most sewage treatment plants. Emergency sewage treatment plants have been built in the meantime (GA, 2021). In the Erft region 7 out of 31 wastewater facilities had been destroyed. Many facilities reported pollution of oil and diesel, forming layers up to 15 cm thick (Kuhn, 2021). In addition, much of the groundwater (and soil) in the flood region was mixed with oil (from destroyed residential oil tanks), chemicals such as fertilizers (from wineries and other agriculture) and chemicals from nearby industrial plants.\n",
