      "In Atlantic waters, upstream of the drain, an extensive dorsal was located, which was moving eastwards, thus increasing the circulation of the wind at the height of the north component, which helped to intensify the jet of entry into the void. In turn, its jet of exit was losing intensity after the cyclogenetic process, thus starting an imbalance between the two, favoring the displacement to the south of the depression in height, in which intense rotating activity was maintained.\n",
