      "Chunk text:  At this moment the jet of entry of the dorsal was weakened by the west-northwest, while its jet of exit was intensified by the interaction of the latter with the subtropical jet, developing an intense southwest circulation whose interaction with the mountainous system of the Atlas led to the formation of a low surface pressure to the undersea of Alborán (Figure 2.3).The formation and subsequent development of this low induced the intensification of the circulation of east component wind on the Mediterranean peninsular facade, bringing moisture to this region. Meanwhile, the jet of southwest component in height induced on the south and the eastern peninsular half an important dynamic forcing that helped to the ascent of the mass of humid air of Mediterranean origin and to the organization of the convection developed after these ascents. In turn, a center of low pressures in surface on the area of the Gulf of Cadiz was formed, so that the dana technically passed to be defined from then on as isolated cold drunkness (BFA).\n",
