      "Chunk text:  From the evening of the 29th and throughout the 30th day, the displacement of the current dorsal above the BFA continued towards the European continent, entering the British islands and extending later to the north and center of Europe. With this height pattern, high over the north of Europe and low over the south-west of Europe, a classic pattern of atmospheric blockade, known as the Rex (Rex. 1950) pattern, was configured and maintained the following days.A fundamental feature of the blocking patterns is the establishment of a jet in height of eastern component, which is in general contrary to the prevailing direction of the west in our latitudes. On this occasion, the intensity of the pressure centers in height favored an east jet at the entrance of the BFA that provided sufficient energy for the maintenance of the depression in height (Figure 2.4). On the other hand, during this period of time, a repositioning of the center of the BFA, moving towards the Atlantic, to the west of Portugal, and thus shifting the area of the greatest atmospheric instability towards the southwestern quadrant peninsular.\n",
