d low over the south-west of Europe, a classic pattern of atmospheric blockade, known as the Rex (Rex. 1950) pattern, was configured and maintained the following days.A fundamental feature of the blocking patterns is the establishment of a jet in height of eastern component, which is in general contrary to the prevailing direction of the west in our latitudes. On this occasion, the intensity of the pressure centers in height favored an east jet at the entrance of the BFA that provided sufficient energy for the maintenance of the depression in height (Figure 2.4). On the other hand, during this period of time, a repositioning of the center of the BFA, moving towards the Atlantic, to the west of Portugal, and thus shifting the area of the greatest atmospheric instability towards the southwestern quadrant peninsular.'}\n",
