      "Processing chunk no. 10 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  During the following days, the dorsal that ran along the north of the dana, slowly surrounded it and curving to the south by its eastern flank, acquiring this axis with a northwest-southeastern orientation. This resulted in the jet of entry to the depressive system acquiring a southeast component that contributed to the deformation of the cold core in height and the weakening of the low surface that ended up disappearing in the early hours of Saturday, November 2.From this moment, technically, the depressive structure went back to being defined as dana. On the other hand, the slow decrease of the intensity of the input jet to the southeast component dana, which in the morning of day 3 was 50 knots, as well as the increase of the intensity of its output jet (of almost 80 knots), was shifting its center towards the center-southeastern peninsular (figure 2.5, above), beginning its phase of dissipation.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 11 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  Finally, the intensification of a dorsal area along the peninsular south contributed even more to the narrowing of the dana and its displacement to the north, which ended up leaving our territory in the northeast of the peninsula on the 4th (Figure 2.5, below), leaving Catalonia with a remarkable dynamic forcing that contributed to the strong rainfall recorded in this autonomous community during the first half of Monday, November 4.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 12 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  In this section, the characteristics of the most relevant stormy structures that occurred between October 28 and November 4 are presented. For each one of them the instant of beginning and end is indicated, the type of structure, the provinces to which it affected or through which it transited, the most adverse surface effects, as well as a brief description. All the hours indicated in this section are referred to the Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) that in winter time is one hour before the official time of the peninsula (2 hours less in summer).The identified convective structures have been labeled according to the classification of convective systems described in Gallis et al. (2008): Belonging to the meso-, meso-, etc. scale. They are characterized by the consecutive development of new cells along the front of the racha. Their average duration is around 1-3 hours.The length of their yuncques is 50-100 km and do not present stratiform precipitation.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 13 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  The possible effects on the surface are hail less than 5 cm, sudden floods, tasted, and lower lendicts of category.A supercell is a single-cell storm that presents a deep and persistent upward current in rotation (mesocyclone) and two downward currents: that of the front flank (FFD), the main and most extensive, and that of the rear flank (RFD), which is smaller and more concentrated. Its average duration is around 1-3 hours. They spread anomalously, shifting to the right of the middle flow (cyclonic or right to move), or to the left (anticyclonic or left to move). Its appearance is ellipsoid in satellite images and 'gancho' or 'coma' in radar images. The length of its anvils is usually in the range 20-150 km. The possible surface effects are hail greater than 2 cm, tornado EF2-EF5, winds greater than 100 km/h, sudden flooding.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 14 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  HP types (High Precipitation), LP (Low Precipitation) and classical. When they form several in the same environment, they are sometimes organized in line or cluster. They can result from a storm.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 15 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  They are storm systems that produce a contiguous (convective or stratiform) precipitation area of the order of 100 km or more in the horizontal scale in at least one direction. They are composed of a large number of individual cells whose proximity causes interactions between them. These individual cells share elements of the cloud system, of the precipitation volume and of the cold air bag ( cold-pool).Its typical duration is 3-24 hours. Due to its size and duration are affected by the acceleration of Coriolis. The length of the semi-highest axis is around 100-500 km.\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 16 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  They can be classified into the following subtypes: Each structure has been labelled taking into account the type of convective structure it presents, the day of the month in which it had its greatest impact, and a number indicating its order of formation on the day in question, so that the first structure on 29 October, which was a convective system of mesoscale, is the SCM29-I, while the third of that day, which were multicells, is the MC29-III. In those cases where structures of different types coexist in the same area simultaneously, they will be labeled as a single precipitating structure by the acronyms EP (e. EP28-III).\n",
      "Getting geolocations of CI assets \n",
      "No CI_TYPE entities found in this chunk. Going to next chunk\n",
      "\n",
      "Processing chunk no. 17 / 94 of document: AEMET 2024 - ESTUDIO SOBRE LA SITUACIÓN DE LLUVIAS INTENSAS.pdf\n",
      "Chunk text:  Valencia/Zaragoza In this section the most intense episodes of precipitation that occurred during the period covered by this study are described day by day.The various events have been selected from among a good number of them based on their derived impacts.\n",
      "The section is structured into different subsections, each corresponding to the day in which the episodes took place. Each subsection is structured into different sections with reference to the names of the most affected autonomous communities. Within each of the sections is shown a description detailing the most affected areas, the period of the day in which precipitation occurred, as well as some observed data from the network of AEMET stations. The notices issued for the different affected areas are also presented in summary form.\n",
      "Table 4.1 summarizes a chronology of the events treated in this section for the different affected autonomous communities. In addition, most of the elements of the table show the type of stormy structure, listed in the previous section, which causes the most prominent precipitations of each selected episode.\n",
