      "Chunk text:  100 ? During the early morning of the day 28 a line of storms (SCM28-I) was sweeping Mallorca from southeast to northeast, initially affecting the south and then east and northeast of the island. It rained throughout the island, although the most affected areas were the south and east. In Manacor, which was the place with the most precipitation collected, the maximum intensity occurred at about 3:00 hours. The squalls presented intensity between very strong and torrential, being observed accumulated in an hour between 50 and 70 mm.\n",
